 "summary": "No Mathlib or Tau Ceti declaration glues finite-rank cores along a morphism or gives a manifold-domain `C^n` inverse of operator families over a subfield; the nearest are `ContMDiffWithinAt.clm_bundle_inverse` (Hom-bundle, same field, VectorBundle/Hom.lean:461), `ContDiffWithinAt.clm_inverse` (normed-space form, Analysis/Calculus/ContinuousLinearMapInverse.lean:216) and the intertwiner-specific `contMDiffOn_inverse_intertwiner`. The PR reuses `CoordinateHom.invOfIsInvertible`, `operator_isInvertible_iff`, `continuousOn_inChartCoordinates`, `clm_inverse_of_eventually_isInvertible`, `IsInvertible.contDiffAt_map_inverse` and `piCongrLeft`/`finCongr` where they apply.",
